{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggtvDdvNHXkxANFru2oB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Dq ≈ 2188 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 459 cm⁻¹, C ≈ 2425 cm⁻¹ (C/B ≈ 5.3)**\n\nI used the d² Tanabe–Sugano energy expressions. The energy zero is the ³F barycentre, and the ground state is ³T₁(F).\n\n**Dq from ³T₂.** The ³T₁(F) → ³T₂ transition is exactly 8Dq, so 8Dq = 17 500 cm⁻¹ and Dq = 2187.5 cm⁻¹.\n\n**B from ³T₁(2).** The two ³T₁ terms mix through the matrix\n\n[[−6Dq, 6B], [6B, 15B + 2Dq]]\n\n- The eigenvalues are 7.5B − 2Dq ∓ S, where S = √[(7.5B + 4Dq)² + 36B²].\n- The ³T₁(F) → ³T₁(2) transition is the difference between the two eigenvalues, 2S. Setting 2S = 25 000 gives S = 12 500 cm⁻¹.\n- Substituting Dq = 2187.5 gives (7.5B + 8750)² + 36B² = 12 500².\n- This simplifies to 92.25B² + 131 250B − 79.69×10⁶ = 0, whose positive root is B ≈ 459 cm⁻¹.\n\n**C from ¹E.** The ¹E term lies at 10B + 2C − 6Dq on the same energy scale, and the ground state lies at 7.5B − 2Dq − S. The ³T₁(F) → ¹E transition is therefore:\n\nν = 2.5B + 2C − 4Dq + S = 9748 cm⁻¹\n\n- Substituting B = 459, Dq = 2187.5 and S = 12 500 gives 1148 + 2C − 8750 + 12 500 = 9748.\n- Solving gives 2C ≈ 4850, so C ≈ 2425 cm⁻¹.\n\n{\"Dq\": 2187.5, \"B\": 459, \"C\": 2425, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Three observed bands determine Dq, B and C via d2 Tanabe-Sugano expressions (³T₂, ³T₁ mixing, ¹E).\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":839,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":839,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d2e3720-17bb-4807-9d07-84501cd1eb0a","uuid":"bfc18b0a-b398-4a0b-88fd-a0e4ebe9a460","timestamp":"2026-11